urce-question-section-content\"><div class=\"source-section-content-wrapper\"><p>Complete the flow chart below.</p><p>Write NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS for each answer.</p><p><b>Expertise in creative writing</b></p><p>Background—researcher had previously studies <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">31</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-practice-source-5-t4-l-q31\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span></p><p>↓</p><p>had initial idea for research-inspired by a book (the <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">32</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-practice-source-5-t4-l-q32\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span> of a well-known novelist).</p><p>↓</p><p>Posed initial question—why do some people become experts while others don't?</p><p>↓</p><p>read expertise research in different fields, avoided studies carried out in a <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">33</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-practice-source-5-t4-l-q33\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span> because they're too controlled.</p><p>↓</p><p>most helpful studies—research into <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">34</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-practice-source-5-t4-l-q34\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span> e.g. waiting tables.</p><p>↓</p><p>found participants: four true <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">35</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-practice-source-5-t4-l-q35\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span> in creative writing (easy to find) and four with extensive experience</p><p>↓</p><p>adopting 'think aloud' techniques to collect <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">36</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-practice-source-5-t4-l-q36\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span> data from inexperience writer. (during session-assistant made <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">37</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-practice-source-5-t4-l-q37\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span> recordings).</p><p>↓</p><p>gathered similar data from experienced writers</p><p>↓</p><p>compared two sets of data and generated a <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">38</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-practice-source-5-t4-l-q38\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span> for analysis (identified five major stages in writing-will be refined later).</p><p>↓</p><p>got an expert <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">39</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-practice-source-5-t4-l-q39\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span> to evaluate the quality of the different products</p><p>↓</p><p>identified the most effective <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">40</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-practice-source-5-t4-l-q40\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span> of stages in producing text.</p></div></div><div class=\"source-questions\"><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div></div>","sourceQuestionCount":10}],"audio_fallbacks":["https://engnovate.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/recent_actual_test_5_academic_listening_test_4_4.mp3"],"order_index":4}],"questions":[{"id":"en-practice-source-5-t4-l-q1","part_id":"en-practice-source-5-t4-l-p1","group_id":"en-practice-source-5-t4-l-g1-0","question_type":"multiple_choice","ieltsQuestionType":"multiple_choice_single","question_text":"","correct_answer":"B",